#N canvas 20 20 7000 5230 12;
#X text 20 20 state-bench -- the data store acceptance run. MOST OF THE DATA STORE IS DELIBERATELY INVISIBLE -- state is FILES \, and test/gate/state-assert.sh proves the logic headlessly in twelve seconds. What is left here is only what hardware can show: the front-panel Save \, a REAL power cycle \, and the mode lamp. Six steps rather than a padded twenty \, because a bench proves the cases it contains and nothing else. STEPPED BY HAND: press GO to run the step that has just been described \, press GO again to describe the next one. Nothing moves until you ask it to \, so the PASS IF is on screen and STILL while you read it. The prompt line always says what the next press will do., f 120;
#X text 20 150 GO ON THE MAC: the bng below \, or the dev panel's ENCODER CLICK -- u_mother-stub sends encbut unconditionally and nothing in Cut It consumes it. TURNING the encoder repeats the current step without advancing \, which is what to do when you looked away., f 120;
#X text 2400 200 ⚠️ GO ON THE DEVICE IS NOT THE ENCODER -- IT IS netcat \, AND THE DIFFERENCE IS NOT OPTIONAL. mother only forwards encbut once a patch has asked with /enableEncoder \, and NOTHING IN Cut It EVER ASKS -- m_organelle leaves the encoder out on purpose. So the click that drives this bench on the Mac is silently dead on the Organelle. Send instead with ./test/run.sh --bench <name> from the Mac. ⚠️ NOT netcat: the line this file used to print does nothing on macOS -- BSD nc exits before the datagram is flushed at -w0 \, and -w1 was measured to fail too \, while the port IS bound and the bench is fine. It looks exactly like a dead bench. The device cannot send to itself either: busybox here has no nc at all. Asking mother to enable the encoder is NOT the fix either: that means writing to oscOut \, and g_oled is its sole owner., f 120;
#X text 20 280 Load it as a THIRD patch after mother.pd and main.pd. It touches nothing in the deployed patch -- it only pushes onto the same buses a controller would. A PASS IF is printed for EVERY step including the ones whose correct result is that nothing happens \, which are otherwise impossible to mark off., f 120;
#X text 2400 20 ON THE MAC EVERY ERROR STEP ALSO PRINTS /sdcard/cut-it-err.cur: write failed \, AND THAT IS NOT A FAILED STEP. u_err keeps its durable log on the Organelle's SD card \, which no Mac has -- so the write is attempted and refused every time. It is in fact the only proof off-device that the logging path ran at all. On the device that line must NOT appear \, and if it does the card is unwritable and the log is being lost silently., f 120;
#X obj 6000 40 r \$0-say;
#X obj 6000 100 print;
#X text 20 360 GO -- click here \, or the dev panel's encoder button. MAC ONLY -- on the device use netcat \, top right., f 60;
#X obj 20 420 bng 40 250 50 0 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -262144 -1 -1;
#X obj 20 500 s \$0-go;
#X obj 300 420 r encbut;
#X obj 300 480 select 1;
#X obj 300 540 t b;
#X obj 300 600 s \$0-go;
#X text 560 480 encbut sends 1 THEN 0 \, so select 1 is what stops one press counting twice., f 46;
#X obj 300 680 netreceive 9998 1;
#X obj 300 740 route go;
#X obj 300 800 t b;
#X obj 300 860 s \$0-go;
#X obj 1400 420 r enc;
#X obj 1400 480 t b;
#X obj 1400 540 s \$0-repeat;
#X text 1660 480 enc is 1 for up and 0 for down -- not plus or minus one -- so either direction repeats., f 46;
#X text 20 920 THE STATE MACHINE. phase 0 means the step has been described and not yet run \; phase 1 means it has run. SETTING THE STEP NUMBER IS WHAT DESCRIBES IT \, so advancing is just an increment -- there is no second path to keep in step., f 120;
#X obj 20 980 r \$0-go;
#X obj 20 1040 f;
#X obj 20 1100 select 0 1;
#X obj 300 1040 r \$0-set-phase;
#X obj 20 1170 t b b;
#X msg 300 1230 1;
#X obj 300 1290 s \$0-set-phase;
#X obj 20 1290 f;
#X obj 20 1350 s \$0-do-run;
#X obj 900 1170 t b b;
#X msg 1180 1230 0;
#X obj 1180 1290 s \$0-set-phase;
#X obj 900 1350 f;
#X obj 900 1410 + 1;
#X obj 900 1470 s \$0-set-step;
#X obj 1700 980 r \$0-set-step;
#X obj 1700 1040 t f f f;
#X obj 1700 1110 s \$0-set-inc;
#X obj 1980 1110 s \$0-set-run;
#X obj 1180 1350 r \$0-set-inc;
#X obj 300 1410 r \$0-set-run;
#X obj 2260 1110 s \$0-do-show;
#X obj 2100 980 r \$0-repeat;
#X obj 2100 1040 s \$0-do-show;
#X obj 2500 980 loadbang;
#X obj 2500 1040 del 500;
#X msg 2500 1100 1;
#X obj 2500 1160 s \$0-set-step;
#X text 20 1920 DESCRIBING A STEP. One select per step rather than one wide fan \, so every cord stays short and local -- the same reason u_map chains its routes., f 120;
#X obj 20 2020 r \$0-do-show;
#X obj 20 2080 select 1;
#X obj 240 2080 t b b b;
#X msg 700 2080 === STEP-01-of-05 === Baseline -- the patch has just booted and nothing has been touched;
#X msg 700 2130 PASS IF: The Launchpad top row shows exactly ONE lit mode lamp. WHICH one is the test: a fresh install comes up on mode-1 and a restored one comes up wherever you left it. If the grid is dark then the Launchpad is not owned and nothing below can be read.;
#X msg 700 2180 >>> press GO to run step 1 of 5;
#X obj 240 2250 s \$0-say;
#X obj 20 2340 select 2;
#X obj 240 2340 t b b b;
#X msg 700 2340 === STEP-02-of-05 === Change the mode -- press transport key 4 on the nanoKONTROL;
#X msg 700 2390 PASS IF: The lit lamp moves to the fourth position. Nothing about STATE is visible yet and that is correct. u_state has it in memory and flushes within two seconds.;
#X msg 700 2440 >>> press GO to run step 2 of 5;
#X obj 240 2510 s \$0-say;
#X obj 20 2600 select 3;
#X obj 240 2600 t b b b;
#X msg 700 2600 === STEP-03-of-05 === Confirm it reached the disk -- from the Mac run ./tools/fetch-state.sh --show;
#X msg 700 2650 PASS IF: cut-it-auto.txt reads mode perform mode-4. THE FILE IS THE ONLY EVIDENCE. Nothing on the instrument displays what has been saved and that is deliberate. If it still reads the old mode then the flush is not firing.;
#X msg 700 2700 >>> press GO to run step 3 of 5;
#X obj 240 2770 s \$0-say;
#X obj 20 2860 select 4;
#X obj 240 2860 t b b b;
#X msg 700 2860 === STEP-04-of-05 === Commit -- on the Organelle press Storage then Save;
#X msg 700 2910 PASS IF: The screen shows Saving briefly and returns. Then cut-it-manual.txt has a NEW timestamp even though it is still empty -- no shipped contributor uses the manual policy yet. An UNCHANGED timestamp means saveState never arrived and the commit path is dead.;
#X msg 700 2960 >>> press GO to run step 4 of 5;
#X obj 240 3030 s \$0-say;
#X obj 20 3120 select 5;
#X obj 240 3120 t b b b;
#X msg 700 3120 === STEP-05-of-05 === The one that matters -- power cycle the Organelle and wait for it to come back;
#X msg 700 3170 PASS IF: The same mode lamp is lit as before the power cycle. This is the only durability test that counts. A patch reload proves nothing about an SD card. DO THIS LAST IN A SESSION because it resets the wifi fault uptime clock and that fault needs about three hours to appear.;
#X msg 700 3220 >>> press GO to run step 5 of 5;
#X obj 240 3290 s \$0-say;
#X obj 20 3380 t b;
#X msg 240 3380 === BENCH COMPLETE === every step has been run -- reload the patch to go round again;
#X obj 240 3440 s \$0-say;
#X text 20 3520 RUNNING A STEP. The actions fire in the order they are listed -- rightmost trigger outlet first -- and the line saying the step has fired goes out LAST \, off outlet 0 \, so it cannot arrive before the thing it describes., f 120;
#X obj 20 3620 r \$0-do-run;
#X obj 20 3680 select 1;
#X obj 240 3680 t b;
#X msg 480 3750 --- step 1 fired --- judge it against the PASS IF above --- press GO for step 2;
#X obj 240 3810 s \$0-say;
#X obj 20 3930 select 2;
#X obj 240 3930 t b;
#X msg 480 4000 --- step 2 fired --- judge it against the PASS IF above --- press GO for step 3;
#X obj 240 4060 s \$0-say;
#X obj 20 4180 select 3;
#X obj 240 4180 t b;
#X msg 480 4250 --- step 3 fired --- judge it against the PASS IF above --- press GO for step 4;
#X obj 240 4310 s \$0-say;
#X obj 20 4430 select 4;
#X obj 240 4430 t b;
#X msg 480 4500 --- step 4 fired --- judge it against the PASS IF above --- press GO for step 5;
#X obj 240 4560 s \$0-say;
#X obj 20 4680 select 5;
#X obj 240 4680 t b;
#X msg 480 4750 --- step 5 fired --- that was the last one --- press GO to finish;
#X obj 240 4810 s \$0-say;
